  "narrative": {
    "intro": "South Carolina had $102M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The state recorded 282 awards with an average award size of $360K. Obligations fell 99.0% year over year. Fiscal-year history shows much larger totals in recent years: FY22 was $7.2B, FY23 was $10.1B, FY24 was $10.6B, FY25 was $8.3B, and FY26 was $9.9B. Current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date. Couriers and Express Delivery Services led industry obligations with $25.9M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $25.5M. The Department of Veterans Affairs, the Department of Energy, and the Department of Justice were the top three buyers by obligation amount in FY2027 to date. BATTELLE SAVANNAH RIVER ALLIANCE, LLC, FEDERAL EXPRESS CORPORATION, and FEDEX SUPPLY CHAIN DISTRIBUTION SYSTEM, INC. were the three largest vendors by obligations in FY2027 to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "South Carolina had $102M in obligations in FY2027 to date versus $9.9B in FY26. FY24 was $10.6B and FY23 was $10.1B. FY22 and FY25 were $7.2B and $8.3B respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries dominated FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $71.5M and the Department of Energy obligated $25.5M in FY2027 to date. Couriers and Express Delivery Services accounted for $25.9M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $25.5M. BATTELLE SAVANNAH RIVER ALLIANCE, LLC received $25.5M and FEDERAL EXPRESS CORPORATION received $25.1M in obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
